! edge — AS65100  (Arista EOS)
!
! Internet edge router.
! - eBGP to ISP (AS65500): receives default route, advertises 198.51.100.0/24
! - OSPF area 0 toward core1 and core2
! - Redistributes BGP default into OSPF via "default-information originate always"
! - Loopback: 10.0.0.1/32
!
hostname edge
!
ip routing
!
interface Loopback0
   description router-id
   ip address 10.0.0.1/32
!
interface Ethernet1
   description to-isp  203.0.113.0/30
   no switchport
   ip address 203.0.113.2/30
   no shutdown
!
interface Ethernet2
   description to-core1  10.255.1.0/30
   no switchport
   ip address 10.255.1.1/30
   no shutdown
!
interface Ethernet3
   description to-core2  10.255.2.0/30
   no switchport
   ip address 10.255.2.1/30
   no shutdown
!
! ================================================
! edge  —  Capstone Tasks
!
! Role: Internet edge router — OSPF area 0 backbone + eBGP to ISP
!
! Task 1 — OSPF Area 0
!   Configure OSPF process 1, make Ethernet1 (WAN) passive, activate
!   Ethernet2/3 (to core1/core2), advertise loopback + both core links
!   in area 0, and inject a default route into OSPF.
!   Hint:
!     router ospf 1
!        router-id 10.0.0.1
!        passive-interface default
!        no passive-interface Ethernet2
!        no passive-interface Ethernet3
!        network 10.0.0.1/32 area 0.0.0.0
!        network 10.255.1.0/30 area 0.0.0.0
!        network 10.255.2.0/30 area 0.0.0.0
!        default-information originate always
!
! Task 2 — BGP prefix-list + route-map
!   Define a prefix-list matching the enterprise public block and a
!   route-map to apply it outbound toward the ISP.
!   Hint:
!     ip prefix-list ENTERPRISE-OUT seq 10 permit 198.51.100.0/24
!     route-map BGP-TO-ISP permit 10
!        match ip address prefix-list ENTERPRISE-OUT
!
! Task 3 — eBGP to ISP + originate enterprise prefix
!   Add a black-hole static route so BGP can originate 198.51.100.0/24,
!   configure router bgp 65100, peer with the ISP, and apply the
!   outbound route-map.
!   Hint:
!     ip route 198.51.100.0/24 Null0
!     router bgp 65100
!        router-id 10.0.0.1
!        no bgp ebgp-requires-policy
!        neighbor 203.0.113.1 remote-as 65500
!        neighbor 203.0.113.1 description isp
!        address-family ipv4
!           neighbor 203.0.113.1 activate
!           neighbor 203.0.113.1 route-map BGP-TO-ISP out
!           network 198.51.100.0/24
! ================================================
!
end
